  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri. Dileep. D. N vs The Union Of India on 13 September, 2024 Author: Hemant Chandangoudar Bench: Hemant Chandangoudar -1- Nc: 2024:Khc:38574 Wp No. 12224 of 2023 In The High Court Of Karnataka At Bengaluru Dated This The 13Th Day Of September, 2024 Before The Hon'Ble Mr Justice Hemant Chandangoudar Writ Petition No. 12224 Of 2023 (Gm-Res) Between: Sri. Dileep. D. N. S/O. Narayanappa Diguveedhi, Aged About 33 Years, Proprietor Of M/S. Dnv Filling Station, No.44/5, Panthanahalli Village, Kyasamballi Hobli, K.G.F. Taluk, Kolar District. ...Petitioner (By Sri. Ramesha B M., Advocate) And: 1. The Union Of India Department Of Ministry Of Petroleum And Natural Gas, Shastri Bhavan, New Delhi-110 001. Rep By Its Secretary. Digitally signed by R Hemalatha Location: High 2. The Union Of India Court Of Rep By Secretary Karnataka Department Of Petroleum And Explosive Safety Organization (Peso) A-1/A-2 Wing, 5Th Floor C.G.O. Complex, C.B.D. Belapur Navi Mumbai-400 614. Sri. Dileep. D. N vs The Union Of India on 13 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/157764562/ 1 3. The State Of Karnataka Rep By Chief Secretary Vikasa Soudha, Bangalore-560 001. 4. The State Of Karnataka Rep By Secretary -2- Nc: 2024:Khc:38574 Wp No. 12224 of 2023 Department Of Food And Civil Supplies Vikasa Soudha, Bangalore-560 001. 5. The Deputy Director Department Of Food And Civil Supplies Kolar District Kolar-563 116. ...Respondents (By Sri. Suresh H S., Advocate For R1 & R2; Sri. Shamanth Naik, Hcgp For R3 To R5) This Writ Petition Is Filed Under Articles 226 And 227 Of The Constitution Of India Praying To Directing The R-5 To Consider The Applications Filed By The Petitioner For Issue Of No Objection Certificate To Run The Bio Diesel (B100) Vide Annx-T. This Petition, Coming On For Preliminary Hearing, This Day, Order WAS MADE THEREIN AS UNDER: CORAM: HON'BLE MR JUSTICE HEMANT CHANDANGOUDAR ORAL ORDER 3. Heard the learned counsel for the parties. 4. The Petroleum and Explosives Safety Organization (PESO), Government of India, issued a communication dated 1.12.2014, NC: 2024:KHC:38574 stating that methyl ester is not a petroleum product and does not fall under the provisions of the Petroleum Rules, 2002. Sri. Dileep. D. N vs The Union Of India on 13 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/157764562/ 2 5.",
    "facts": "Respondents No. 1 and 2 have also filed a statement of objections, stating that Bio-Diesel/methyl ester does not come under the purview of petroleum products and, therefore, does not attract the provisions of the Petroleum Rules, 2002. As a result, suspending the sale of Bio-Diesel on the grounds that the petitioner has not obtained permission is legally unsustainable. Furthermore, the first respondent lacks the authority to suspend the sale of Bio-Diesel when it does not fall under the purview of petroleum products, and the Petroleum Rules, 2002, do not apply. Therefore, the impugned cancellation/suspension of Bio-Diesel sales lacks authority and is not legally sustainable.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
